[0.010, "o", "claude-mm\r\ncodex-mm\r\nlib\r\nminimax\r\n"]
[0.502, "o", "\r\n$ codex-mm --profile demo --help | sed -n '1,70p'\r\n"]
[0.023, "o", "Notice: ignoring --profile; this wrapper pins MiniMax config directly.\r\n"]
[0.093, "o", "Codex CLI\r\n\r\nIf no subcommand is specified, options will be forwarded to the interactive CLI.\r\n\r\nUsage: codex [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]\r\n       codex [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGS]\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  exec        Run Codex non-interactively [aliases: e]\r\n  review      Run a code review non-interactively\r\n  login       Manage login\r\n  logout      Remove stored authentication credentials\r\n  mcp         Manage external MCP servers for Codex\r\n  mcp-server  Start Codex as an MCP server (stdio)\r\n  app-server  [experimental] Run the app server or related tooling\r\n  app         Launch the Codex desktop app (downloads the macOS installer if\r\n              missing)\r\n  completion  Generate shell completion scripts\r\n  sandbox     Run commands within a Codex-provided sandbox\r\n  debug       Debugging tools\r\n  apply       Apply the latest diff produced by Codex agent as a `git apply` to\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "              your local working tree [aliases: a]\r\n  resume      Resume a previous interactive session (picker by default; use\r\n              --last to continue the most recent)\r\n  fork        Fork a previous interactive session (picker by default; use --last\r\n              to fork the most recent)\r\n  cloud       [EXPERIMENTAL] Browse tasks from Codex Cloud and apply changes\r\n              locally\r\n  features    Inspect feature flags\r\n  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\nArguments:\r\n  [PROMPT]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Optional user prompt to start the session\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  -c, --config <key=value>\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Override a configuration value that would otherwise be loaded from\r\n          `~/.codex/config.toml`. Use a dotted path (`foo.bar.baz`) to override\r\n          nested values. The `value` portion is parsed as TOML. If it fails to\r\n          parse as TOML, the raw string is used as a literal.\r\n          \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Examples: - `-c model=\"o3\"` - `-c\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          'sandbox_permissions=[\"disk-full-read-access\"]'` - `-c\r\n          shell_environment_policy.inherit=all`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "      --enable <FEATURE>\r\n          Enable a feature (repeatable). Equivalent to `-c features.<name>=true`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "      --disable <FEATURE>\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Disable a feature (repeatable). Equivalent to `-c\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          features.<name>=false`\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  -i, --image <FILE>...\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Optional image(s) to attach to the initial prompt\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  -m, --model <MODEL>\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Model the agent should use\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "      --oss\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Convenience flag to select the local open source model provider.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Equivalent to -c model_provider=oss; verifies a local LM Studio or\r\n          Ollama server is running\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n      --local-provider <OSS_PROVIDER>\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Specify which local provider to use (lmstudio or ollama). If not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          specified with --oss, will use config default or show selection\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  -p, --profile <CONFIG_PROFILE>\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "          Configuration profile from config.toml to specify default options\r\n"]
[0.509, "o", "\r\n$ minimax codex --help | sed -n '1,35p'\r\n"]
[0.084, "o", "Codex CLI\r\n\r\nIf no subcommand is specified, options will be forwarded to the interactive CLI.\r\n\r\nUsage: codex [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]\r\n       codex [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGS]\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  exec        Run Codex non-interactively [aliases: e]\r\n  review      Run a code review non-interactively\r\n  login       Manage login\r\n  logout      Remove stored authentication credentials\r\n  mcp         Manage external MCP servers for Codex\r\n  mcp-server  Start Codex as an MCP server (stdio)\r\n  app-server  [experimental] Run the app server or related tooling\r\n  app         Launch the Codex desktop app (downloads the macOS installer if\r\n              missing)\r\n  completion  Generate shell completion scripts\r\n  sandbox     Run commands within a Codex-provided sandbox\r\n  debug       Debugging tools\r\n  apply       Apply the latest diff produced by Codex agent as a `git apply` to\r\n              your local working tree [aliases: a]\r\n  resume      Resume a previous interactive session (picker by default; use\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "              --last to continue the most recent)\r\n  fork        Fork a previous interactive session (picker by default; use --last\r\n              to fork the most recent)\r\n  cloud       [EXPERIMENTAL] Browse tasks from Codex Cloud and apply changes\r\n              locally\r\n  features    Inspect feature flags\r\n  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\nArguments:\r\n  [PROMPT]\r\n          Optional user prompt to start the session\r\n\r\n"]
[0.511, "o", "\r\nDemo complete.\r\n"]
